                [ 'p', 'For an invitation you print the motif and the guest’s name, and the laser immediately cuts a lace edge – without moving the sheet between a printer and a cutter. xTool even sells envelopes made of paper for M2 printing, intended among other things for invitations. According to the manufacturer, a 40 ml CMYK cartridge lasts for up to 400 pages, and the CleanCut panel helps with through-cuts. Thick board and large batches of boxes, however, take the M2 longer than a CO₂ laser.' ],
                [ 'products', '15452856942805,9372812673237,9570646196437' ],
                [ 'h3', 'xTool S1: larger sheets in an enclosed machine' ],
